WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
After a storm, a stream can run brown with mud.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.680
Where does that mud come from?

3
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.680
Two trays of soil and a watering can will show you.

4
00:00:12.633 --> 00:00:16.513
Once the trays are ready, the test takes about thirty-five minutes.

5
00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:22.313
Your child makes a guess and compares the cups after giving both trays the same

6
00:00:22.313 --> 00:00:25.913
rain. They practice explaining what the cups show.

7
00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:28.457
Stay with your child throughout.

8
00:00:29.777 --> 00:00:32.197
Use bagged soil and plain, untreated seed.

9
00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:36.077
Sow it thickly in one tray two to three weeks ahead.

10
00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:38.877
Keep it moist in a sunny spot.

11
00:00:40.037 --> 00:00:41.937
Or press sod into the tray that day.

12
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:46.600
Fill the bare tray with bagged soil about five centimeters deep.

13
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.020
If you grew grass from seed, use the same bagged soil in both trays.

14
00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.440
You cut a small notch at the low end of each.

15
00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.300
Raise the other ends on books, to the same height.

16
00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.540
Set a clear plastic cup under each notch.

17
00:01:03.583 --> 00:01:06.403
Give both trays the same slope and the same rain.

18
00:01:07.703 --> 00:01:10.063
One tray is bare, and the other has grass.

19
00:01:11.503 --> 00:01:13.723
Ask your child, 'Which cup will get more mud?'

20
00:01:14.323 --> 00:01:15.743
Write the guess down before you pour.

21
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.940
For gentle rain, hold the watering can about twenty centimeters above the high end.

22
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.480
Pour two cups over about thirty seconds.

23
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.060
Repeat with the same amount, height, and speed.

24
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.160
What do you predict the cups will look like?

25
00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:40.313
The bare tray's runoff is usually cloudier.

26
00:01:41.573 --> 00:01:43.913
The grass tray's cup often has less water.

27
00:01:45.313 --> 00:01:47.433
Ask, 'Where did the soil in this cup come from?'

28
00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:52.753
Check the guess. After ten minutes, measure the settled soil with a ruler.

29
00:01:53.900 --> 00:02:00.180
Empty the cups. Pour two fresh cups onto each tray, taking about five seconds per

30
00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.520
tray. Look for small channels called rills.

31
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.640
After ten minutes, measure the settled soil again.

32
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.920
Lift the grass with a spoon to see the roots.

33
00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:15.627
Leaves and stems soften the impact of falling drops.

34
00:02:17.007 --> 00:02:19.367
Roots grip the soil and help water soak in.

35
00:02:20.627 --> 00:02:23.367
On bare soil, raindrops can knock grains loose.

36
00:02:24.787 --> 00:02:28.007
Water flowing downhill can carry those grains into the cup.

37
00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.390
Stay with your child.

38
00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.670
You do the cutting and lift the wet trays.

39
00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:38.150
Keep small pieces and seed away from children under four.

40
00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.930
Call nine one one if choking.

41
00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.510
Never taste plants, soil, or seed.

42
00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.930
Wash hands with soap and water afterward.

43
00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:53.550
For an optional walk, check the weather and choose shade or use sun protection.

44
00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:58.750
Wait until rain stops and at least thirty minutes after the last thunder.

45
00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.690
Stay together on a dry path where you have permission.

46
00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.950
Stay away from roads, storm drains, steep crumbling banks, and bodies of water.

47
00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.750
Never walk through floodwater.

48
00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.270
At a bare patch, ask, 'How could we fix it?'

49
00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:16.830
Check for ticks afterward.

50
00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:21.910
Wash hands with soap and water after handling soil or plants.
